{
  "$comment": [
    "FROZEN GATES — a clause is offered behind a control that no intake answer can move.",
    "",
    "The blueprint reads as a choice and the document is a constant. Nothing in any clause,",
    "requirement or baseline is wrong, which is why every earlier check was blind to it.",
    "",
    "A frozen control that is TRUE means the user cannot decline the clause. A frozen control",
    "that is NULL/UNDEFINED/FALSE means the user can never obtain it: the clause is authored,",
    "cited, reviewed and unreachable.",
    "",
    "disposition is an AUTHORING decision, never derived:",
    "  WIRE      the control should be answerable — add or connect the intake question",
    "  DELETE    the family always needs the clause — remove the gate, it is decoration",
    "  INTENDED  the control is correctly constant for this family and the gate is harmless",
    "  NOT_REVIEWED  nobody has decided yet. The honest default.",
    "",
    "This inventory covers ALL families. An earlier version of the guard checked three, and",
    "reported 7 of these 50 — the engine/knowledge separation exists to prevent exactly that:",
    "gate reachability is an engine property and must be checked wherever gates exist.",
    "",
    "Regenerate with: node tests/gateReachability.test.mjs --write"
  ],
